# Purpose: Sort a last-name-first supplier roster so it can be reviewed and filed consistently.
# Inputs: vendors/contacts.txt: one comma-separated last-name, first-name, email row per contact.
# Outputs: exports/supplier-contacts-sorted.csv: alphabetized contact rows; stdout echoes the roster.
accept contacts_path as text with default "vendors/contacts.txt"
run mkdir with flags ["-p"] and paths ["exports"]
run cat with path contacts_path
pipe to sort
then save to "exports/supplier-contacts-sorted.csv"
